  "title": "Erdős Problem #1122",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $f:\\mathbb{N}\\to \\mathbb{R}$ be an additive function (i.e. $f(ab)=f(a)+f(b)$ whenever $(a,b)=1$). Let $ A=\\{ n \\geq 1: f(n+1)< f(n)\\}. $ If $\\lvert A\\cap [1,X]\\rvert =o(X)$ then must $f(n)=c\\log n$ for some $c\\in \\mathbb{R}$?",
